# Keep the append-only record append-only across merges.
#
# Every branch adds an entry at the top of the progress log, so two branches in
# flight conflict on the same line every time — always resolved by keeping both.
# `merge=union` does that automatically. It is safe here *only* because the file
# holds nothing mutable: the status table that used to live at its top now sits
# in docs/status.md, where a union merge would have duplicated rows instead of
# merging them.
#
# Caveat worth knowing: union merge never raises a conflict, so it will not tell
# you the two entries interleaved out of order. Check newest-first after a merge.
docs/progress-log.md merge=union

# Dart source is text, and git must be told so rather than sniffing for it.
#
# Git calls a blob binary when it finds a NUL in the first 8000 bytes. That is
# a heuristic about content, not about language, so a stray control byte in a
# `.dart` file turns the whole file into `Bin 1234 -> 5678 bytes` — no diff, no
# blame, no review. `lib/app/sync/sync_tables.dart` spent this branch that way.
#
# This fixes the *display*. It does not stop the byte getting in; the
# `text-encoding` CI job is what does that.
#
# The attribute is `diff` **set**, not `diff=text`. The latter names a custom
# diff driver, which would have to be defined in git config and is not; the
# bare form is git's documented "treat as text even when it contains bytes that
# normally never appear in text files".
*.dart diff
*.sql diff
